WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.993
Hello, I'm Maria Rigatoni. Welcome to Italy, and welcome to my house.

2
00:00:06.994 --> 00:00:11.008
In Italy there is so much to see and so much to do.

3
00:00:11.009 --> 00:00:14.423
But best of all, there is so much to eat.

4
00:00:14.424 --> 00:00:19.149
Italy is famous for pizza, pasta, and the world's best ice cream.

5
00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:24.583
Today I will be making spaghetti with tomato sauce for lunch.

6
00:00:24.584 --> 00:00:28.631
The first thing we need to do is to make a nice pile of flour.

7
00:00:28.632 --> 00:00:32.209
Then we make a big hole in the top of our pile.

8
00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:35.599
Just like this. It's for the eggs.

9
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:39.285
Now carefully we crack four eggs into the hole.

10
00:00:39.286 --> 00:00:42.566
Add just a little bit of water, not too much.

11
00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:46.930
Next we mix all the ingredients together.

12
00:00:46.931 --> 00:00:51.022
Now you have to knead the dough. This is the hard part.

13
00:00:51.023 --> 00:00:55.372
You have to push and fold, push and fold, push and fold.

14
00:00:55.373 --> 00:00:58.845
Keep kneading! It makes your hands sore.

15
00:00:58.846 --> 00:01:03.050
Now the dough is perfect, but it has to sit for thirty minutes.

16
00:01:03.051 --> 00:01:05.986
While we wait, I'll tell you a story.

17
00:01:05.987 --> 00:01:11.837
In the thirteenth century, there was an Italian man named Marco Polo.

18
00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:15.725
He was a great explorer and a famous Italian.

19
00:01:15.726 --> 00:01:23.000
When Marco was only 14 years old, his father decided to go on a voyage of exploration.

20
00:01:23.001 --> 00:01:28.793
Marco begged his father to take him along, and finally his father agreed.

21
00:01:28.794 --> 00:01:34.381
They traveled all the way to China and they had great adventures.

22
00:01:34.382 --> 00:01:42.182
During their voyage, Marco saw many things that Italians had never seen before, such as eyeglasses and ice cream.

23
00:01:42.183 --> 00:01:46.033
But best of all, he discovered long, thin noodles.

24
00:01:46.034 --> 00:01:51.871
Marco Polo brought these noodles to Italy, and we called them spaghetti.

25
00:01:51.872 --> 00:02:01.295
Some historians claim that Marco Polo discovered noodles in the Arab world, and historians still debate whether he really discovered them in China.

26
00:02:01.296 --> 00:02:10.180
Nonetheless, it is widely accepted by the Italians that spaghetti noodles were first imported to Italy from China.

27
00:02:10.181 --> 00:02:15.611
Okay, we are ready for the next step. This is my pasta maker.

28
00:02:15.612 --> 00:02:18.416
Today I'll use it to make spaghetti noodles.

29
00:02:18.417 --> 00:02:21.747
We take our dough and put it in the pasta maker.

30
00:02:21.748 --> 00:02:27.299
Then presto! We have long, thin lines of spaghetti.

31
00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:30.020
Next we have to boil the spaghetti.

32
00:02:30.021 --> 00:02:33.973
We take our noodles and carefully put them into boiling water.

33
00:02:33.974 --> 00:02:39.182
Now we have to wait for ten minutes, so I will tell you another story.

34
00:02:39.183 --> 00:02:41.598
Do you see this tomato sauce?

35
00:02:41.599 --> 00:02:46.991
When we serve this on top of spaghetti, it tastes delicious.

36
00:02:46.992 --> 00:02:56.016
We make this sauce by boiling tomatoes, other vegetables, and spices for many, many hours―sometimes as long as one day.

37
00:02:56.017 --> 00:03:00.349
But did you know that at one time we didn't have tomatoes in Italy?

38
00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:04.266
Tomatoes had to come from Mexico.

39
00:03:04.267 --> 00:03:10.087
In the sixteenth century, the people who explored Mexico found fresh tomatoes.

40
00:03:10.088 --> 00:03:15.071
Because they were so delicious, they decided to bring some back to Europe.

41
00:03:15.072 --> 00:03:19.510
Soon we began to grow tomatoes in Italy.

42
00:03:19.511 --> 00:03:24.678
Because of the warm sun and good soil, tomatoes grew very well in Italy.

43
00:03:24.679 --> 00:03:28.476
So we began making many kinds of foods from tomatoes.

44
00:03:28.477 --> 00:03:32.312
Tomato sauce is now the most famous Italian sauce.

45
00:03:32.313 --> 00:03:36.825
It is used for spaghetti and pizza.

46
00:03:36.826 --> 00:03:43.137
Ah, the spaghetti is ready. Now we pour the hot noodles into the strainer.

47
00:03:43.138 --> 00:03:48.159
Then we put them on a plate. Last, we add some tomato sauce.

48
00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:56.595
And here you are, Mrs. Rigatoni's spaghetti. Mangia! Mangia!

